record(s,t,rs,decs,inv,'The page contains cancelled Kummer and H³ fragments, local-cohomology case tables, the Z–Q–Q/Z sequence and two further sequences with marginal identifications. The source’s comment reads “pas de miracle, car les deux sont nuls.” The last H³(Ubar,G_m)=0 identification carries a question mark. The connecting degree was inspected because the cohomological sequence suggests i+1, but the tiny ink stroke remains ambiguous and has not been replaced by that expectation. The heavily retraced first zero and the fragmented marks after the first long sequence remain doubtful.\n\n177.N1: For the displayed Z–Q–Q/Z sequence, the usual maps are the inclusion j:Z→Q and quotient q:Q→Q/Z. The inclusion has zero kernel; q(a)=0 exactly for a∈Z, so ker(q)=im(j); every coset has a rational representative, so q is onto. This checks that algebraic sequence, and supplies no proof of the page’s cohomology calculations. Archive number 176; no date.',doubts=[['177','connecting exponent',r'\unsure{i+1|i-1}','plus / bent minus','low'],['177','end of first long sequence',r'\unsure{\cdots}','fragmented marks; no secure continuation object','low'],['177','i=0 in global case table',r'\unsure{0}','heavily retraced oval','low']],notation=[['Sheaf cohomology symbol',r'\uline{H}^i_x','177','Separate underline; the global Hⁱ_S display has no corresponding line.'],['Barred schemes in bottom sequences',r'\bar X,\bar U','177','The bars occur at every X/U in the two bottom sequences; the preceding sentence has bar X and unbarred U.']],hand=['The isolated μ is live: its close parallel uprights are letter strokes, while the cancelled μ_n line above has a long transverse strike. H cancels the isolated occurrence.','The zero at i=0 is repeatedly looped and stays doubtful; other zeros on this page are small ovals.','In the right-hand note, the phrase pas de miracle recurs from scan 174, but was checked on its own crop. The final nuls has a high l loop.'],abbreviations=[['inv.','invariants']],events=[['177.N1','targeted proof check','Checked exactness of Z→Q→Q/Z using the inclusion and quotient maps, by their kernels and coset representatives. No cohomology result was proved.']],extra='Certainty-only checks: bar X in the last sequence resolves M0074 on crop 177 (323,1963,410,2046); M0071 and M0073 remain open on their recorded crops. H’s certain i+1 and 0 have the same first candidates as C, so certainty alone creates no collation row. The scattered marks are reproduced without assigning them an additional word, formula or cancellation. The lower label has two underlines; it is not transcribed as a double arrow.')
